Previously, I had done a sabermetric breakdown of a plate appearance in the Wild Card game between BOS @ NYY this season, and now I wanted to do one for a PA that I believe we all remember from the 2024 ALCS. A game where Juan Soto became the hero for the “Bronx Bombers” and carried NYY to the World Series that same season.

Cleveland struck first in Game 5, scoring one run in the 2nd inning and another in the 5th. NYY responded quickly with two runs to tie the game in the 6th, and no runs were scored over the next two and a half innings. The game went to extra innings, bringing us to the top of the 10th inning at Progressive Field.

