The CLE manager called on Hunter Gaddis to face Anthony Volpe and the bottom of the Yankees lineup, assuming he could get through the next three hitters quickly. And that’s exactly what happened with Anthony Volpe, who was retired in three pitches with a lineout to shortstop.

