Then Alex Verdugo came up for his 4th PA, with Wells on first. Verdugo saw only two pitches, and the second was an 83.4 MPH changeup (CH) that Verdugo read well and hit toward second base. The second baseman fielded it cleanly and threw to the shortstop covering second for the out, but the ball slipped out of his hand at the bag, and the final ruling was fielder’s choice. Verdugo reached safely at first.

